From bc11a5598e70637bd5c3722e5ebb6005c00c44b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aleksei Bukhalov <buhaloff.aleks@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 13:11:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] fix: disk search() must find a true common-prefix
 match, not just whole-key equality

DiskPromptStore.search()'s 'shorter'/'longer' checks required one
sequence's entire stored length to equal-or-prefix the other exactly.
This missed the common case in this project's own frozen chat-shaped
workload: a stored assistant-turn entry is [wrapped user prompt]
[generated continuation], and the next turn's query extends only the
user-prompt portion with its own different continuation -- the two
diverge partway through, well before either one's own full length, even
though a large, valid, and very usable common prefix exists between
them.

Confirmed live on M4 (Gate G1-MLX rerun after removing eager
restore-on-start in the previous commit): a query that should recover
6553/6896 tokens (matching the original Gate G1-MLX receipt, where RAM's
own PromptTrie -- which computes a true longest-common-prefix as a
natural byproduct of walking token-by-token -- found this match)
recovered 0 via this method against the exact same disk-resident entry,
because the entry's own stored length (6606) was never reached before
the two diverged at token 6553. Eager restore's bulk RAM preload routed
every post-restart lookup through the trie and happened to mask this gap
for as long as it existed; removing it sent every on_miss lookup through
this method directly, exposing it.

search()'s 'longer' case now tracks the best true LCP-based trimmable
candidate (covering both a literal superset and a same-or-shorter
partial-divergent match); consult_and_promote recomputes and uses that
real common-prefix depth instead of assuming the query's own full length
minus one is always safe to trim to. The cost-model admission check now
also covers this generalized trimmable case (only the recoverable delta
beyond what RAM already had), not just the old 'shorter' branch, so a
small partial match still has to clear its own read cost. Live-verified
against the exact repro (isolated 11-turn session replay): fixed run
recovers 6553/6896 tokens in 4.46s, versus 0/6896 in 22.5s before this
fix, matching the original run 3 receipt's 6553-token recovery.
